From: ROCm/rocm-systems upstream repair
Subject: [PATCH] Remove CQ_THREAD_STACK_SIZE and use the system default stack

Linux/glibc puts a process's initial ELF TLS in each pthread stack mapping.
A fixed 256 KiB mapping can be smaller than a valid client's TLS alone;
pthread_create then returns EINVAL before the worker entry point executes.
Full CUDA/HIP clients can encounter this during graph instantiation when a
diagnostic kernel creates a hostcall listener. Command-queue workers also
consume this stack contract outside direct dispatch. This is not thread
exhaustion or a device error.

Backport the three CLR changes from upstream commit
ccc4faf7c7517f3e970ac849cc77f38a41d4f45a (ROCm/rocm-systems#9643).
Both consumers use amd::Thread's existing native-default stack contract;
the TLS-incompatible flag is removed rather than kept as a second authority.
Graph capture, queue counts, packet publication and dispatch concurrency
are unchanged. The upstream hostcall tests are outside this runtime-only
build; Llaminar registers its captured timeline/TLS proof in preflight.

Pinned base: ROCm/rocm-systems 6b0e43f341195e203754e08f850e437ff2fc09f9
             (therock-10.0, ROCm Core SDK 10.0.0)
Upstream: https://github.com/ROCm/rocm-systems/commit/ccc4faf7c7517f3e970ac849cc77f38a41d4f45a

diff --git a/rocclr/device/devhostcall.cpp b/rocclr/device/devhostcall.cpp
--- a/rocclr/device/devhostcall.cpp
+++ b/rocclr/device/devhostcall.cpp
@@ -334,7 +334,10 @@ class HostcallListener {
 #endif
   class Thread : public amd::Thread {
    public:
-    Thread() : amd::Thread("Hostcall Listener Thread", CQ_THREAD_STACK_SIZE) {}
+    // Take the system default stack: glibc allocates a thread's static TLS block inside the stack
+    // requested through pthread_attr_setstacksize() and refuses the request when the two do not
+    // fit, which is easy to hit from a process that links libraries with large PT_TLS segments.
+    Thread() : amd::Thread("Hostcall Listener Thread") {}
 
     //! The hostcall listener thread entry point.
     void run(void* data) {
diff --git a/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp b/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp
--- a/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp
+++ b/rocclr/platform/commandqueue.hpp
@@ -152,7 +152,8 @@ class HostQueue : public CommandQueue {
 
     //! Create a new thread
     Thread()
-        : amd::Thread("Command Queue Thread", CQ_THREAD_STACK_SIZE, !AMD_DIRECT_DISPATCH),
+        : amd::Thread("Command Queue Thread", 0 /* use the system default stack size */,
+                      !AMD_DIRECT_DISPATCH),
           acceptingCommands_(false),
           virtualDevice_(nullptr) {}
 
diff --git a/rocclr/utils/flags.hpp b/rocclr/utils/flags.hpp
--- a/rocclr/utils/flags.hpp
+++ b/rocclr/utils/flags.hpp
@@ -22,8 +22,6 @@ release(bool, AMD_LOG_ASYNC, true,
         "Async logging with in-memory buffer and background thread (set 0 to disable)")\
 debug(uint, DEBUG_GPU_FLAGS, 0,                                               \
         "The debug options for GPU device")                                   \
-release(size_t, CQ_THREAD_STACK_SIZE, 256*Ki, /* @todo: that much! */         \
-        "The default command queue thread stack size")                        \
 release(int, GPU_MAX_WORKGROUP_SIZE, 0,                                       \
         "Maximum number of workitems in a workgroup for GPU, 0 -use default") \
 debug(bool, CPU_MEMORY_GUARD_PAGES, false,                                    \
